WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.644
KL doesn't group from scratch; it improves an existing bisection.

2
00:00:08.644 --> 00:00:13.667
This chapter's seed is AE | BCD, cut 12.

3
00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:19.133
The only move: swap one from each side; the side sizes stay.

4
00:00:19.533 --> 00:00:23.533
First, each node's external and internal weight.

5
00:00:23.533 --> 00:00:28.333
D = external − internal: A is +6, C is −4.

6
00:00:28.333 --> 00:00:33.356
D is how much the cut drops if that node alone moves.

7
00:00:33.756 --> 00:00:38.778
A pair swap's gain: the two D values added, minus 2w.

8
00:00:38.778 --> 00:00:45.800
Both D values count E–D as external, and it stays cut after the swap, so it comes off twice.

9
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:51.489
Of the six candidates A↔D is largest, +9; E↔D is −1.

10
00:00:51.889 --> 00:00:57.133
One pass: pick the largest-gain pair, swap, lock, recompute D.

11
00:00:57.133 --> 00:01:01.267
Step 1, A↔D: cut 12 → 3.

12
00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:07.844
At step 2 every gain is negative; take E↔C anyway: the cut rises to 11.

13
00:01:07.844 --> 00:01:12.200
No movable node is left on the left; the trials end.

14
00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:16.289
Cumulative gains: 0, +9, +1.

15
00:01:16.289 --> 00:01:22.200
The largest is k = 1: from the start, apply only A↔D, cut 3.

16
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:26.333
Step 2 is undone: a trial is not an acceptance.

17
00:01:26.733 --> 00:01:31.089
Pass 2 starts from cut 3, everything unlocked.

18
00:01:31.089 --> 00:01:35.667
Cumulative −8, −6: neither beats doing nothing.

19
00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:39.600
The empty prefix wins, and the algorithm stops.

20
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.133
Four things to keep.

21
00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:46.267
One for one, sizes fixed; the gain loses 2w;

22
00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:50.533
try negative gains too, accept only the best prefix.

23
00:01:50.533 --> 00:01:54.889
Step through every trial in the lab below.
